KG42.register("source_edge_archive-66d4ad5f367ad6b9b4423823",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E002","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","rule_ref":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E002","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.supply","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","target":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","source_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","target_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","source_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::coordination.price_signal","target_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::bidding.supply","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Aggregate producer supply feasibility and RCI treatment of power boundaries. | Information exchanged by producers with their neighboring negotiating agents during RCI. | Producer bilateral supply quantities in MBED and their RCI updates. | Producer quantity updates in the decentralized RCI implementation of MBED. | The direct-solution approach discussed for MBED local subproblems. | Within-iteration ordering of RCI updates for producers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"44ee2df3eb243f247c27fb78511b8100fcadc0c169b5f0bb6898baad597d7cbd","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"M01","source_definition":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity. The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor. Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration. The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence. Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","target_definition":"Price-signal coordination supplies the perceived-price input to the inverse-gradient target power setpoint used in updating the producer's bilateral offered quantity. Scope: Producer quantity updates in the decentralized RCI implementation of MBED. Condition: Agent n operates as a producer during an RCI iteration. Updating the trading-price dual variables precedes updating the producer's bilateral offered quantities; power-boundary dual updates also occur before the quantity-update step. Scope: Within-iteration ordering of RCI updates for producers. Condition: Each RCI iteration containing the producer P-update. Different price offers lead the producer to try to concentrate its offered quantity with the neighboring agent having the most interesting price and offer nothing to the others; the source describes direct-solution outcomes as usually binary. Scope: The direct-solution approach discussed for MBED local subproblems. Condition: A producer's local subproblem is solved directly with different offered trade prices. Each bilateral offered quantity is constrained to be nonnegative. The producer P-update enforces this sign restriction through its max operator at each iteration. Scope: Producer bilateral supply quantities in MBED and their RCI updates. Condition: Agent n operates as a producer. The sum of a producer's bilateral offered quantities is subject to its lower and upper power-injection bounds. RCI enforces the power-boundary constraints through Lagrangian relaxation. Scope: Aggregate producer supply feasibility and RCI treatment of power boundaries. Condition: Producer quantities must satisfy the bounds at a feasible MBED solution; the RCI implementation treats these constraints through Lagrangian relaxation. A producer must send its current bilateral offered quantity to the corresponding neighboring agent as part of the prescribed quantity-and-price information bundle. Scope: Information exchanged by producers with their neighboring negotiating agents during RCI. Condition: At each RCI iteration.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Updating the trading-price dual variables precedes updating the producer's bilateral offered quantities; power-boundary dual updates also occur before the quantity-update step. Scope: Within-iteration ordering of RCI updates for producers. Condition: Each RCI iteration containing the producer P-update.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e15"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e28","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"problem at iteration k presented in (10) can be expressed as Llocn (pn, λkn, μn, μn) = Cn(pn) + Cn(p","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For any trade between two agents n and m, we define a new price, referred to as the perceived price, through λ̂_nm = λ_nm − c_nm (16) By opposition, the trading reciprocity constraint dual variables (λ_nm) are referred to as trading prices. As an example, in a tax implementation of product differentiation, the perceived price corresponds to the price after tax, while trading prices correspond to the price before tax."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e33","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-A. Structure of the Method","anchor_text":"prFig. 2. Flowchart of the relaxed consensus + innovation algorithm. from the others. This results i","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 2","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"An iteration of the Relaxed Consensus + Innovation method can be split into three steps. The first two steps consist in updating the dual variables of the trading reciprocity constraints and of the power boundary constraints (III-B). The third step consists in updating the decision variables based on a gradient step built on optimality conditions of the local optimality problem (III-C). Some operational aspects are presented in III-D. The structure of the algorithm is summed up in Fig. 2."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"SORIN et al.: CONSENSUS-BASED APPROACH TO PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY MARK The Lagrangian of the relaxe","equation_id":"(19)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The primal variables are then updated following (19), referred to as P-update (here for a producer),\n  P nmk+1 = max  0, P nmk + fnmk  P n(m),k+1 −P nk       (19)\n... The max operator in (19) is used to enforce the sign constraint of the decision variables and is replaced in the case of a consumer by a min operator."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Aggregate producer supply feasibility and RCI treatment of power boundaries. | Information exchanged by producers with their neighboring negotiating agents during RCI. | Producer bilateral supply quantities in MBED and their RCI updates. | Producer quantity updates in the decentralized RCI implementation of MBED. | The direct-solution approach discussed for MBED local subproblems. | Within-iteration ordering of RCI updates for producers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E002","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.supply","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"paper_scope_note":"The λ update, P update, and required communication of RCI have direct formula basis; only protocol component dependencies are allowed, and the values of k and k+1 or the roles of consumer and producer are not conflated."}});
